1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,460
Let's review what we learned in this lesson.

2
00:00:02,460 --> 00:00:05,735
Once your product has been built, you're done.

3
00:00:05,735 --> 00:00:08,165
Wait, not so fast.

4
00:00:08,165 --> 00:00:09,905
There's still more work to do.

5
00:00:09,905 --> 00:00:12,050
After the product has been built,

6
00:00:12,050 --> 00:00:14,415
it's important to validate that it's working well

7
00:00:14,415 --> 00:00:17,565
and providing value for users before launching it.

8
00:00:17,565 --> 00:00:20,270
We talked about how you can partner with

9
00:00:20,270 --> 00:00:23,350
the QA team to collaborate on writing test plans.

10
00:00:23,350 --> 00:00:26,750
In particular we talked about how test cases need to

11
00:00:26,750 --> 00:00:30,680
be defined for both functional and non-functional requirements.

12
00:00:30,680 --> 00:00:35,900
This type of testing will validate if the product is working correctly as intended.

13
00:00:35,900 --> 00:00:39,500
We also talked about how to run a dogfood program and

14
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:42,710
dogfooders can be a great source of additional feedback.

15
00:00:42,710 --> 00:00:45,560
Dogfooders can help to answer the question of

16
00:00:45,560 --> 00:00:49,480
how well your product works under real-world conditions.

17
00:00:49,480 --> 00:00:55,580
At this point you'll have a lot of different feedback from QA testing and dogfood.

18
00:00:55,580 --> 00:01:00,260
We talked about how to prioritize issues based on severity.

19
00:01:00,260 --> 00:01:03,920
There's a limited amount of time you and your team have everyday

20
00:01:03,920 --> 00:01:08,010
to get things done but a never ending list of to-dos.

21
00:01:08,010 --> 00:01:11,870
It's important to think about value versus effort to make sure you're

22
00:01:11,870 --> 00:01:15,995
spending your time on the things that are going to make the biggest impact.

23
00:01:15,995 --> 00:01:19,695
Lastly, we talked about go/no go meetings.

24
00:01:19,695 --> 00:01:22,695
Why they're valuable and how to run one.

25
00:01:22,695 --> 00:01:27,110
This meeting is important because it makes sure everyone is on the same page

26
00:01:27,110 --> 00:01:31,455
about the state of the product and if the decision is go,

27
00:01:31,455 --> 00:01:33,465
you get to move on to launch.

28
00:01:33,465 --> 00:01:35,590
But if the decision is no go,

29
00:01:35,590 --> 00:01:39,510
then there's more work to do before launching.

